Z||000014||Monkeyman||09-16-2000||04:00 PM||||Gold-86SE--I've been to WalMarts in most of the 49 states you can get to with a truck.  I've only bought guns in a couple of them, but I've seen signs in just about all of them that say something to the effect that you have to be 18 and they want to see some picture ID.  I've never heard of anyone having to go through any red tape other than that although I don't live in the Lone Star state so I don't know their laws specifically.  If you had to do that, I believe you, but it must be a Texas law only.  It's not Federal and it's not that way in most states.  21 for a handgun and 18 for just about everything else (other than GT Bastards assault weapon, of course <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).||||reg||1
